    "+ 1 added",
    "Totals: + 1, ~ 0, - 0, → 0",
    "Specs updated successfully.",
    "Change 'add-greeting-name' archived as '<date>-add-greeting-name'.",
  ],
  "removed": [
    "openspec/changes/add-greeting-name/.openspec.yaml",
    "openspec/changes/add-greeting-name/design.md",
    "openspec/changes/add-greeting-name/proposal.md",
    "openspec/changes/add-greeting-name/review.md",
    "openspec/changes/add-greeting-name/specs/greeting/spec.md",
    "openspec/changes/add-greeting-name/tasks.md",
  ],
  "written": {
    "openspec/changes/archive/<date>-add-greeting-name/.openspec.yaml": 
"schema: story
created: <date>
"
,
    "openspec/changes/archive/<date>-add-greeting-name/design.md": 
"## Context

See \`proposal.md\` and \`specs/greeting/spec.md\`.

## Decisions

- Read the name from the first argument, because it needs no parser.

## Risks / Trade-Offs

- [An empty name] -> Print \`Hello, world!\`.
"
,
    "openspec/changes/archive/<date>-add-greeting-name/proposal.md": 
"## Why

A user wants the greeting to use their name.

## What Changes

- The greeting takes an optional name.

## Capabilities

### New Capabilities

- \`greeting\`: print a greeting for a name

### Modified Capabilities

None.

## Impact

\`src/greet.ts\` and its tests.
"
,
    "openspec/changes/archive/<date>-add-greeting-name/review.md": 
"## Agreement

- [x] Each capability of the proposal has a spec
- [x] Each requirement has a scenario
- [x] The design covers each requirement
- [x] No \`[NEEDS CLARIFICATION\` marker is open

## Gaps

None.
"
,
    "openspec/changes/archive/<date>-add-greeting-name/specs/greeting/spec.md": 
"## Purpose

The greeting prints a short hello message for a person or for the world.

## ADDED Requirements

### Requirement: Greeting with a Name

The system SHALL print \`Hello, <name>!\` when the user gives a name.

#### Scenario: A Name Is Given

- **WHEN** the user runs the command with the name \`Ada\`
- **THEN** the output is \`Hello, Ada!\`
"
,
    "openspec/changes/archive/<date>-add-greeting-name/tasks.md": 
"## 1. Greeting

- [ ] 1.1 Add the name argument, and verify it with \`just check\`
"
,
    "openspec/specs/greeting/spec.md": 
"# greeting Specification

## Purpose
The greeting prints a short hello message for a person or for the world.

## Requirements

### Requirement: Greeting with a Name

The system SHALL print \`Hello, <name>!\` when the user gives a name.

#### Scenario: A Name Is Given

- **WHEN** the user runs the command with the name \`Ada\`
- **THEN** the output is \`Hello, Ada!\`
"
,
  },
}
`;

